		{
			dependencies: ["2182B348FE0E32CA"]
			description: [
				"The Spatial IO Port is the heart of any Spatial IO setup. It controls the cut-and-paste operation that moves entire areas into the spatial storage dimension. It displays important stats like energy usage, required capacity, and setup efficiency. Insert a properly sized Spatial Storage Cell into its input slot and give the port a redstone pulse to swap the defined volume with whatever is saved in the cell."
				""
				"BE CAREFUL: Any entities inside the defined area will also be moved, so make sure you have a way out before hitting the switch!"
				""
				"For detailed setup instructions, multiblock requirements, and tips on choosing cell dimensions, check out the full Spatial IO section of the guide."
			]
